## Reception

::bg{location="reception" time="night"}
@narrator{code="0010"}: A switchboard with its cords pulled out and laid in a neat row, like the switchboard itself had been laid out for viewing.
@narrator{code="0020"}: A duty roster is still pinned to the corkboard. The drawer under the desk is not quite shut.
@narrator{code="0030"}: Through the wall, the pharmacy door has a keypad of its own, four digits, green letters that read PRESCRIBED STAFF ONLY.
<match on="run.hour">
  <when is="h23|h00">
    @nell{code="0010" mono}: The clock above the desk says half past four. It has said half past four since 1979.
  </when>
  <otherwise>
    @nell{code="0020" mono}: The clock above the desk says half past four. For the first time tonight, that feels close.
  </otherwise>
</match>
